# .alchemy.env - control-plane credentials, shared by all apps and stages.
#
# Required for CI deploys and `pnpm db:query`. Optional for manual deploys once
# you have run `alchemy login`. Never loaded by `pnpm dev`. Mechanism and CI
# round-trip: docs/deploy.md
#
# Copy to `.alchemy.env` and fill in. Gitignored - never commit real secrets.
#
#   FOO=      fill this in
#   # FOO=    optional

# Cloudflare API token - lets alchemy create/update Workers, D1, KV, R2, routes.
#
# Generate: pnpm dlx alchemy util create-cloudflare-token
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# Encryption key for alchemy's remote state store. Must be identical across every saasflare
# project on the same Cloudflare account.
#
# Read by alchemy itself, so a grep of this repo finds no reference. Keep it.
#
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32
ALCHEMY_STATE_TOKEN=

# Pin the target Cloudflare account.
#
# When your credentials can see several accounts, alchemy uses the FIRST one it
# lists and only prints a warning - the usual reason a deploy lands in the wrong
# account. Dashboard -> any domain -> Overview -> Account ID.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# Use a named `alchemy login` profile instead of `default`. Ignored when
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN is set. Profiles live in `~/.alchemy/config.json`.
# ALCHEMY_PROFILE=
